The original distiller-nf provides the Hi-C mapping pipeline: read truncation,
mapping (bwa), pair parsing (pairtools), sorting, binning, and cooler
generation. All credit for that pipeline belongs to the Open2C developers.

Modifications in this repository (Copyright (c) 2026):
  - Restructured the monolithic merge/deduplication stage
    (merge_dedup_splitbam) into a parallel split-apply-combine design
    (sort_group + dedup_group + merge_dedup_final).
  - Fixed a variable-name mismatch in local_truncate.nf.
  - Changed the pairtools dedup walks-policy default to 5unique to
    avoid discarding valid junction-spanning read pairs.

These modifications are released under the same MIT License. The upstream
